# ShedOS sync-configs user exclude list
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/shedos/sync-exclude and edit to taste.
# Paths listed here are excluded from the ShedOS dotfile sync; ShedOS
# will never seed, auto-update, or drop a .shedosnew for them.
#
# If a path already has manifest state or a leftover .shedosnew from
# before you excluded it, the next `shedos-sync-configs` run auto-purges
# those droppings. Your live file in $HOME is never touched.
#
# Format:
#   - One glob per line, matched against the relpath under $HOME
#     (no leading slash).
#   - `#` at the start of a line is a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#   - Trailing/leading whitespace is stripped.
#   - Globs follow bash pattern-matching rules: `*` matches any string
#     (including `/`), `?` matches one char, `[abc]` matches a char class.
#
# The defaults below are always excluded regardless of this file:
#   .config/nvim/lazy-lock.json
#   .config/nvim/lazyvim.json
#   .local/state/*
#   .cache/*
#
# Examples; uncomment or adapt to your setup:

# Keep your own hyprland bindings; don't let upstream drop .shedosnew for them.
#.config/hypr/hyprland.conf

# Ignore everything under a whole directory.
#.config/waybar/*

# Ignore a specific file under a nested tree.
#.config/kitty/current-theme.conf
